From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gregory Mitchell <me@gmitch215.xyz>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 09:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] mm/nommu: free a copied region's pages in aligned blocks

A copied region's pages come out of alloc_pages_exact(), which splits
them, and free_page_series() put each one back on its own. Every page
went through the per-cpu list and was merged into the buddy allocator
separately; in a run of short-lived programs that was more than half of
exit_group.

free_page_series() now takes the references of an aligned block of
pages together (page_ref_freeze, so a page another holder still has is
left to put_page) and hands the block to free_frozen_pages(). A
program's 32-page stack is one block, its 52-page data mapping three.
---
 mm/nommu.c | 28 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 27 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/mm/nommu.c b/mm/nommu.c
index 42aaf7fc9..d08395016 100644
--- a/mm/nommu.c
+++ b/mm/nommu.c
@@ -516,14 +516,40 @@ static void delete_nommu_region(struct vm_region *region)
 
 /*
  * free a contiguous series of pages
+ *
+ * The pages of a copied region come out of alloc_pages_exact() split, so each holds one reference
+ * of its own. A page at a time they go through the per-cpu lists and are merged back one by one,
+ * which was most of an exec'd program's exit. Where the series has an aligned block of pages that
+ * nobody else holds, take their references together and give the buddy allocator the block.
  */
 static void free_page_series(unsigned long from, unsigned long to)
 {
-	for (; from < to; from += PAGE_SIZE) {
+	while (from < to) {
 		struct page *page = virt_to_page((void *)from);
+		unsigned long pfn = page_to_pfn(page);
+		unsigned long left = (to - from) >> PAGE_SHIFT;
+		unsigned int order = min3(pfn ? (unsigned int)__ffs(pfn) : MAX_PAGE_ORDER,
+					  (unsigned int)fls_long(left) - 1,
+					  (unsigned int)MAX_PAGE_ORDER);
+		unsigned long n = 1UL << order;
+		unsigned long i;
+
+		for (i = 0; i < n; i++)
+			if (!page_ref_freeze(page + i, 1))
+				break;
+		if (i == n) {
+			atomic_long_sub(n, &mmap_pages_allocated);
+			free_frozen_pages(page, order);
+			from += n << PAGE_SHIFT;
+			continue;
+		}
 
+		/* another reference somewhere: this page goes the usual way */
+		while (i--)
+			page_ref_unfreeze(page + i, 1);
 		atomic_long_dec(&mmap_pages_allocated);
 		put_page(page);
+		from += PAGE_SIZE;
 	}
 }
 
